### #1 Typed IR (Code Sketch, Local)
Goal: keep display names for diagnostics, but use canonical kinds/handles in IR so backend logic stops parsing/comparing type strings.

```jai
// ir_shared.jai (sketch)
IR_Type_Kind :: enum {
  UNKNOWN;
  BOOL;
  I32; U32;
  I64; U64;
  F32;
  F32x2; F32x3; F32x4;
  F32x2x2;
  STRUCT;
  BUFFER_PTR;   // pointer-to-buffer-element
  FIXED_ARRAY;
}

IR_Type :: struct {
  kind: IR_Type_Kind;
  display_name: string;         // existing text, diagnostics/debug only
  struct_name: string;          // when kind == .STRUCT
  element: *IR_Type;            // pointer/array element types
  array_count: s64;             // when kind == .FIXED_ARRAY
}

IR_Field :: struct {
  name: string;
  type: IR_Type;                // replaces most type_name string checks
  semantic: string;
  original_type_name: string;
  is_pointer: bool;             // migration compatibility
  pointer_pointee_type_name: string; // migration compatibility
  pointer_pointee_is_struct: bool;   // migration compatibility
}

IR_Function_Arg :: struct {
  name: string;
  type: IR_Type;
  is_readonly: bool;
  original_type_name: string;
}

IR_Stmt :: struct {
  // DECL
  decl_type: IR_Type;           // keep decl_type_name temporarily during migration
  decl_type_name: string;
  ...
}
```

```jai
// spirv_text_backend.jai (sketch)
spv_kind_from_ir_type :: (t: IR_Type) -> IR_SPV_Gen_Type {
  if t.kind == .U32 return .UINT;
  if t.kind == .I32 return .INT;
  if t.kind == .I64 return .INT64;
  if t.kind == .U64 return .UINT64;
  if t.kind == .F32 return .FLOAT;
  if t.kind == .F32x2 return .FLOAT2;
  if t.kind == .F32x3 return .FLOAT3;
  if t.kind == .F32x4 return .FLOAT4;
  if t.kind == .F32x2x2 return .FLOAT2X2;
  if t.kind == .BOOL return .BOOL;
  if t.kind == .STRUCT return .STRUCT;
  return .UNKNOWN;
}

helper_arg_is_buffer_pointer :: (arg: IR_Function_Arg) -> bool {
  return arg.type.kind == .BUFFER_PTR;
}
```

Pilot migration surface:
- `IR_Function_Arg.type_name` users in helper inline path
- `IR_Stmt.decl_type_name` users in declaration lowering/emission
- struct-field typing in local-struct allocation and constructor checks

Exit criteria for pilot:
- no `expr_type_from_decl(...)` calls in helper arg binding paths
- pointer helper-arg binding no longer parses `*T` text
- old string fields still present only for printing/debug compatibility

Pilot status:
